        // We cannot directly reference internal recorded balance, so we assert the contrapositive which is observable:
        // If amount > beforeContractBal then withdraw must have reverted (because contract cannot pay more than it holds).
        // This is a general safety: contract cannot send out more than its own Ether balance.

        // Final assert: If amount is greater than the contract's balance before the call, the withdraw call must have reverted.
        assert(!(amount > beforeContractBal) || reverted);
